To further demonstrate how Meta-Debate en-
ables more effective debate configurations, we
present two representative examples from the Math-Vision dataset. In each case, Meta-Debate selects
the most suitable model for a role based on (1) the
model’s knowledge relevant to the question and (2)
its ability to fulfill the intended role function. In
the first example (Question 1), two models propose
to serve as the Affirmative. Proposal 1 contains
a reasoning error, whereas Proposal 2 is fully cor-
rect. During the Meta-Debate stage, our evaluator
assesses reasoning validity and assigns a low score
to the flawed proposal (shown inbold), preventing
it from being selected. Consequently, the proposal
that is both correct and well-reasoned receives a
high score and is chosen as the Affirmative, ulti-
mately leading to a correct debate outcome.
